## Phase 2 — Frontend MVP (Week 2-4)

### Correction #8: Reordered UI Flow

DNA review happens **immediately** after upload — before the interview. This builds instant trust.

| Step | Route | What Happens |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Upload | `/campaign/new` | User uploads a product image |
| 2. Instant AI Analysis | `/campaign/new/analysis` | Vision Adapter extracts draft Product DNA with confidence scores. User sees: *"The AI understood my product."* |
| 3. Review Product DNA | `/campaign/new/review-dna` | User confirms or corrects low-confidence fields |
| 4. Interview | `/campaign/new/interview` | System asks targeted questions (occasion, vibe, target audience) |
| 5. Reference Upload | `/campaign/new/references` | Optional: upload moodboard, logo, past campaigns |
| 6. Creative Objective | `/campaign/new/objective` | Choose objective (Luxury Editorial / Catalog / etc.) |
| 7. Campaign Workspace | `/campaign/{id}` | Generate, review, approve/reject assets |
| 8. Export | `/campaign/{id}/export` | Download approved assets |

### Design Principles
- User **never** sees Knowledge Claims, Physics Ontology, Constraint Solver, or Creative State.
- Collapsible "Engine Room" panel for power users shows the Creative Decision Trace.
- Premium dark UI with glassmorphism — the product must feel luxury-fashion-grade.

